                      (    forth6809.asm):02984         ; NONAME (":NONAME", CORE EXT): like COLON, but deliberately skips
                      (    forth6809.asm):02985         ; HEADER entirely - no WORD call (consumes no name from the input),
                      (    forth6809.asm):02986         ; no new header written at DPHERE, and LATEST is left completely
                      (    forth6809.asm):02987         ; untouched. That's the ANS-required "no-name" definition: never
                      (    forth6809.asm):02988         ; findable by FIND, never linked into the dictionary chain at all.
                      (    forth6809.asm):02989         ; In this subroutine-threaded system the execution token IS the code
                      (    forth6809.asm):02990         ; address (no separate CFA indirection, unlike CREATE's DODOES
                      (    forth6809.asm):02991         ; trampoline), so the xt ANS requires :NONAME to leave on the stack
                      (    forth6809.asm):02992         ; is simply CODEHERE at this instant - identical to what HEREW
                      (    forth6809.asm):02993         ; returns - pushed BEFORE compilation of the body begins, matching
                      (    forth6809.asm):02994         ; where ANS says :NONAME produces it. CSP is snapshotted AFTER that
                      (    forth6809.asm):02995         ; push (mirroring COLON's own CSP snapshot, taken after HEADER's
                      (    forth6809.asm):02996         ; transient pushes/pops have already netted back to baseline) so
                      (    forth6809.asm):02997         ; SEMI's control-flow consistency check at ";" only catches a
                      (    forth6809.asm):02998         ; genuinely unbalanced IF/DO etc. left over from the body, not the
                      (    forth6809.asm):02999         ; xt itself, which is meant to still be there when ";" returns.
                      (    forth6809.asm):03000         ; SEMI itself needs no changes: its unsmudge-the-word-at-LATEST step
                      (    forth6809.asm):03001         ; still targets whatever LATEST already was (the previous NAMED
                      (    forth6809.asm):03002         ; word, untouched by this routine) - a harmless no-op there, since a
                      (    forth6809.asm):03003         ; normal definition is already unsmudged by the time any later
                      (    forth6809.asm):03004         ; definition's SEMI runs.
DFBF DC08             (    forth6809.asm):03005         NONAME:  LDD   CODEHERE
DFC1 3606             (    forth6809.asm):03006                  PSHU  D
DFC3 DD3D             (    forth6809.asm):03007                  STD   CURXT     ; BUG FIX: RECURSE needs this word's own xt
                      (    forth6809.asm):03008                                   ; (see RECURSE and COLON's matching fix) -
                      (    forth6809.asm):03009                                   ; :NONAME deliberately never touches LATEST
                      (    forth6809.asm):03010                                   ; (correctly, per ANS - a :NONAME word is
                      (    forth6809.asm):03011                                   ; never findable/linked), but RECURSE used to
                      (    forth6809.asm):03012                                   ; unconditionally walk LATEST's header to find
                      (    forth6809.asm):03013                                   ; the xt to recurse into. Inside a :NONAME
                      (    forth6809.asm):03014                                   ; body that meant RECURSE compiled a call to
                      (    forth6809.asm):03015                                   ; whatever NAMED word happened to be defined
