                      (    forth6809.asm):04633                                   ; the internal counter hit LEAVE before +LOOP's
                      (    forth6809.asm):04634                                   ; own limit test would otherwise fire reported
                      (    forth6809.asm):04635                                   ; ttester's "WRONG NUMBER OF RESULTS" (one extra
                      (    forth6809.asm):04636                                   ; item), and the leftover item then threw off
                      (    forth6809.asm):04637                                   ; later tests' own stack baselines too. Moved
                      (    forth6809.asm):04638                                   ; PULU D/STD MSCR to the top, unconditionally,
                      (    forth6809.asm):04639                                   ; before the LEAVE check - it's needed on every
                      (    forth6809.asm):04640                                   ; path (LEAVE-exit, boundary-exit, and the
                      (    forth6809.asm):04641                                   ; continue-looping path alike), not just the
                      (    forth6809.asm):04642                                   ; two paths that used to reach it.
