                      (    forth6809.asm):04664                     ; so GD2 and friends still passed - but Annex F's GD8 (its
                      (    forth6809.asm):04665                     ; "ustep"/"step" constants are deliberately sized to march
                      (    forth6809.asm):04666                     ; the index across nearly the whole MAX-UINT/MAX-INT range)
                      (    forth6809.asm):04667                     ; hits the spurious antipodal flip first every time, exiting
                      (    forth6809.asm):04668                     ; at exactly half the correct iteration count (128 instead
                      (    forth6809.asm):04669                     ; of 256) - confirmed by simulating both the old algorithm
                      (    forth6809.asm):04670                     ; and the fix below against GD8's own 4 cases, and checking
                      (    forth6809.asm):04671                     ; the fix still agrees with the old algorithm (and with
                      (    forth6809.asm):04672                     ; hardware-confirmed behavior) on GD2, a limit=0 decreasing
                      (    forth6809.asm):04673                     ; loop, and an exact-landing case, where the two never
                      (    forth6809.asm):04674                     ; differed. Correct, general test: compare old_u and new_u
