F84C                  (    forth6809.asm):07053         SUBSTITUTEW: ; REWRITE: was a plain substring search-and-replace on
                      (    forth6809.asm):07054                      ; the bare registered name (via SEARCHW), which found
                      (    forth6809.asm):07055                      ; "girl" and replaced only that span, leaving surrounding
                      (    forth6809.asm):07056                      ; "%...%" delimiters untouched in the output - and never
                      (    forth6809.asm):07057                      ; returned the substitution count ANS requires as a
                      (    forth6809.asm):07058                      ; third stack item. Per the ANS spec (forth-standard.org/
                      (    forth6809.asm):07059                      ; standard/string/SUBSTITUTE), SUBSTITUTE must scan for
                      (    forth6809.asm):07060                      ; text between '%' (ASCII $25) delimiter pairs
                      (    forth6809.asm):07061                      ; specifically: "%%" collapses to a single '%' (count
                      (    forth6809.asm):07062                      ; unchanged); a name matching the REPLACES registration
                      (    forth6809.asm):07063                      ; has the ENTIRE "%name%" span - delimiters included -
                      (    forth6809.asm):07064                      ; replaced by the substitution text (count incremented);
                      (    forth6809.asm):07065                      ; a non-matching name is passed through unchanged,
                      (    forth6809.asm):07066                      ; delimiters and all (count unchanged); an unpaired
                      (    forth6809.asm):07067                      ; trailing '%' with no closing delimiter passes the
                      (    forth6809.asm):07068                      ; residue through unchanged. Confirmed via MAME testing
                      (    forth6809.asm):07069                      ; against a real template. GLOBALS is fully packed
                      (    forth6809.asm):07070                      ; (256/256), so this reuses MSCR/MSCR2/MSCR3/MSCR4
                      (    forth6809.asm):07071                      ; (confirmed untouched by SUBCOPY) rather than adding
                      (    forth6809.asm):07072                      ; dedicated cells: MSCR = current read position, MSCR2 =
                      (    forth6809.asm):07073                      ; running substitution count, MSCR3/MSCR4 = local scratch
                      (    forth6809.asm):07074                      ; per %-pair found. Reuses the existing COMPAREW for name
                      (    forth6809.asm):07075                      ; matching rather than a new comparison loop.
